  "problem": "Determine the number of local maxima and minima $f(x)$ has on the interval  $x\\in (\\frac{1}{2},5).$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $f(x)$ has \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,$ local maxima and \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,$ local minima.",
  "worked_solution": "We have the derivative \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =-\\frac{2({x}^{2}+2x-8)}{(2{x}^{2}-11x+5)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the critical point $x=2.$ We use the first derivative test to determine whether this point is a local maximum or minimum.\n\nLet's choose the test points $x=1,3$ and evaluate the first derivative at these points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(1) & =-\\frac{2({1}^{2}+2\\cdot 1-8)}{(2\\cdot {1}^{2}-11\\cdot 1+5)^{2}}=\\frac{5}{8}>0 \\\\ {f}^{′}(3) & =-\\frac{2({3}^{2}+2\\cdot 3-8)}{(2\\cdot {3}^{2}-11\\cdot 3+5)^{2}}=-\\frac{7}{50}<0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe summarize the information in the table shown below.\n\n| $x$ | $(\\frac{1}{2},2)$ | $2$ | $(2,5)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Test Point | $1$ |  | $3$ |\n| ${f}^{′}$ | $+$ | $0$ | $-$ |\n| $f$ | $↗$ | max | $↘$ |\n\nFinally, let's use the table above to classify the critical point.\n\n- At $x=2,$ the first derivative changes sign from positive to negative. Therefore, $x=2$ is a local maximum.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $f(x)$ has $1$ local maximum and $0$ local minima on the interval $x\\in (\\frac{1}{2},5).$",
